Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for Musify

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` (v2.0.1) as a dependency in package.json
- Updated package-lock.json with the new dependency

### 2. Configured Analytics in HTML
- Added Vercel Web Analytics script tag to index.html
- Script is loaded from CDN: `https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js`
- Used the `defer` attribute for optimal page load performance
- Placed the script in the `<head>` section after Firebase SDKs

## Files Modified

### index.html
- Added Vercel Web Analytics script tag in the `<head>` section
- Script loads asynchronously with the `defer` attribute to avoid blocking page rendering

### package.json
- Added `@vercel/analytics` as a dependency

### package-lock.json
- Updated with @vercel/analytics dependency information

## Implementation Details

This project is a vanilla HTML/JavaScript application (not React/Next.js), so I followed the official Vercel documentation for HTML-based projects, which recommends using the CDN script tag approach.

The analytics script will automatically:
- Track page views
- Collect visitor analytics
- Send data to Vercel's analytics dashboard
- Work seamlessly once the project is deployed to Vercel

## Next Steps

Once this is deployed to Vercel:
1. The analytics will automatically start collecting data
2. You can view analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab
3. The script will be loaded from `https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js`

No additional configuration is required. The analytics will work automatically once deployed to Vercel.

## Framework Detected
Vanilla HTML/JavaScript project with Python backend (Flask/FastAPI)

## Documentation Reference
Implementation follows the latest Vercel Web Analytics quickstart guide:
https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
